spec:
  grid: fixed 11x11, orange (7) background, pink (6) separators at rows 3,7 and cols 3,7
  structure: 3x3 arrangement of 3x3 cells; separators form a tic-tac-toe frame
  sprites: diamond shape at offsets (0,1),(1,0),(1,2),(2,1) within each 3x3 cell
  center: cell (1,1) always contains a red (2) diamond
  arm: exactly one of the 8 neighboring cells of center contains a red diamond
  mode_A_input: only the 2 red diamonds present (no other sprites)
  mode_A_output: same 11x11 grid with grey (5) and teal (8) diamonds added at positions 135deg CW and CCW from arm direction
  mode_B_input: 2 red + 1 grey + 1 teal diamonds at correct rotational positions
  mode_B_output: 16x16 all-orange grid (4 sprites * 4 pixels = 16)
  rotation_rule: |
    arm direction = arm_pos - center(1,1) mapped to 8-direction index
    grey at direction_index+3 (mod 8), teal at direction_index-3 (mod 8)
  arm_direction: any of 8 neighbors (cardinal and diagonal both observed)
  ratio: 3 of 4 examples are mode A, 1 is mode B [observed]

generation_strategy:
